Subject: [PATCH 351/443] [ae-patch] web: a newer model gets its own picker row
 next to an alias row

An alias row (opus, fable) used to be rewritten to the newer model while keeping its alias id, so the picker said Opus 6 and started the old model. The alias row now stays as it is and a new row for the newer id goes in front of it.
